* TODO write detailed list of differences to R5RS
  - no type or range checks.
  - no overflow-detection.
  - max/min do not change exactness (well, not always - identify cases).
  - primitives are not necessarily "eq?"
  - "set!" of primitive might not necessarily work ("define" is ok, though).
  - 3rd arg to "substring" is optional.
  - behaviour of transcendental functions with regard to nan/inf may be wrong.
  - and more
